From 443785bb33895a93aebcee705ed9c50ef666f4fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:34:57 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 27/63] exl3 cuda: the grouped load-ahead on sm_120 up only,
 bit-equal to main's loop under the contract

warp_tiles takes its load as a template argument: PLAIN is main's loop, AHEAD the tile ahead. tf_exl3_grouped_* build
AHEAD where __CUDA_ARCH__ >= 1200 and PLAIN below, so sm_80, sm_86 and sm_89 compile main's code (their SASS is
main's, instruction for instruction, under nvcc 13.0 and 13.3) and keep main's records under every compiler.
exl3_grouped.cuh holds the projection; contract_controls.cu builds main's loop for each codebook
(tf_ctl_exl3_grouped_old_*) and two planted faults: the next load reads tile i + 2, or the last tile decodes the
words before it.

contract_exl3_grouped.zig registers the three kernels as replacements of main's loop: bit-equal at 1, 2 and 3 k
tiles a warp, at GLM-5.3-Flash's and MiMo-V2.6-Flash's expert widths on one and two ranks and the Qwen3.5 EXL3
pack's, and at the tile edges, with each expert at its own width (lane words 2 and 3). Gate 4 holds the float64
reference's gamma bound on its stress rows (fp16 overflows, bf16 misses 240x; host-tested at the runner's seeds).

Records: sm_80 to sm_89 are main's again (13.0, 13.2's 128 and 13.3's, measured equal); sm_120 and sm_121 carry the
load-ahead's measured registers, 149/157/145 under 13.0 and 158/158/148 under 13.3; 13.2 stays pending there.
